{"id":"u-08066ff8-99b1-4dbb-aa52-b871559a8741","src":"community","title":"Kame Sennin Foundation!","author":"Thomas A.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/GVFHFs-kame-sennin-foundation-1","desc":"Getting powerful.\n\nThis program is designed to build strength, explosiveness, athleticism, and overall physical capability rather than maximizing hypertrophy alone. The emphasis is on moving heavy weight with speed and intent while developing a resilient and well-rounded physique.\n\nMost sets are prescribed using RPE, allowing for autoregulation based on daily performance. As a general guideline, increase the weight by 2.5–5 kg each week on all main lifts, provided the prescribed RPE is maintained.\n\nProgram Structure\n\n* Weeks 1–3: Linear progression using the main exercises, focusing on strength development and technical proficiency.\n* Week 4: An alternative training week featuring different exercises and a slightly higher hypertrophy focus. The goal is to maintain strength while reducing monotony and building additional muscle.\n* Weeks 5–6: Return to the main program and continue the linear progression established in the first three weeks.\n* Week 7: Performance week. Work up to near-maximal lifts, aiming for outstanding performances while keeping a little juice in the tank—heavy, but not all-out maximal attempts.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Powerbuilding","Bodyweight Fitness","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-06T23:54:29.855Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Plyometric Jumps","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8,"x":8}]},{"n":"Zercher Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Box Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Cossack Squat","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"With kettlebell"},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"